spans.s:
DAM, Ⅳ. P. dā́mya, be tame;
 tame, 🞄subdue: pp. dāntá, tame, gentle;
 calm, 🞄tranquil, having oneʼs passions subdued;
 cs. 🞄damáya, P. tame, break in;
 control, subdue: 🞄pp. damita, tamed, subdued.

2. dam-á, a. taming, subduing (—˚);
 m. 🞄self-control;
 punishment, fine;
 Victor, N. of 🞄one of Damayantīʼs brothers and of other men.

dā-ma, n. cord, band;
 garland;
 ā́, f. id.;
 🞄(a) -ka, n. id..

dam-ana, a. (ī) taming, subduing (—˚);
 🞄m. horse-tamer, charioteer;
 Vincent, N. of one 🞄of Damayantīʼs brothers;
 n. subduing;
 chastising.

dambh-a, m. fraud, dissimulation, hypocrisy, 🞄deceit;
 -aka, a. deceiving, deluding 🞄(—˚);
 -ana, a. injuring (—˚);
 n. deceiving, 🞄deceit.

dā́-man, 〈1.〉 n. gift;
 〈2.〉 m. cord, band, 🞄rope;
 bond;
 garland.

dāma‿udara, m. ep. of Viṣṇu or 🞄Kṛṣṇa (having a rope round his belly), so 🞄called because his foster-mother tried to tie 🞄him thus;
 N.: -gupta, m. N. of a poet;
 🞄-araṇya, n. N. of a forest.
